RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
July 19, 2010
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne convened in regular session beginning at 12:00
p.m. in Council Chambers for the purpose of acting upon vouchers for payment as presented.
Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL MEMBERS - Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles,
Ms. Case, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Spiker and Mr. Valdez.  Absent: Ms. Ash, Mr. Collins and Mr. Pierson.
Also present:  Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Dan White, City
Attorney.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.
Mr.Brown moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr. Spiker.
Upon inquiry, Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, provided information available on a voucher payable to
Caribbean Greens, Inc. ($7,337.00), miniature golf course repairs at Taco John’s Events Center.
Motion to approve carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.
Purpose of the meeting having been met, Mayor Kaysen adjourned the meeting at 12:03 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle
July 23, 2010
```
